
========================================================================================================
  P1  THE DEGENERACY IS EXACT IN DEEP MOND -- and the transition breaks it
========================================================================================================
  [OK] P1a the M/L-a0 degeneracy is exact in deep MOND ONLY IF THE WHOLE baryon budget scales with Upsilon: g_obs = sqrt(g_bar a0) is invariant under (g_bar -> L g_bar, a0 -> a0/L), residual 0. That is the textbook statement -- and P1a' shows it does NOT apply to real galaxies
  [OK] P1a' *** THE DEGENERACY IS BROKEN BY THE GAS, AND THIS IS THE CORRECTION MY OWN CONTROL FORCED ON ME. *** With g_bar = Upsilon g_star + g_gas, rescaling Upsilon does NOT rescale g_bar, so the invariance FAILS: residual = sqrt(a_0)*(-sqrt(lam)*sqrt(Upsilon*g_star + g_gas) + sqrt(Upsilon*g_star*lam + g_gas))/sqrt(lam) != 0, collapsing to 0 only when g_gas -> 0. The HI mass is measured from a flux, carries no mass-to-light ratio, and therefore anchors a0 even in the deepest MOND regime. That is why the corpus's gas-dominated a0-line is its sharpest estimator
  [OK] P1b there is a SECOND, independent lever: even with the whole budget scaling, the Newtonian limit multiplies g_obs by lam -- the FULL factor L, not 1. So the transition region breaks the degeneracy on SHAPE alone. Two independent levers, gas fraction and shape, neither needing an SPS model

  size of the lever at the kappa gap (L = 1.08540):
        g_bar/a0   g_obs ratio      dex
            0.01      1.000881  0.00038
            0.10      1.008063  0.00349
            1.00      1.043575  0.01852
           10.00      1.077918  0.03259
          100.00      1.084589  0.03527
  [OK] P1c the lever runs from 1.00001 (deep, blind) to 1.08539 (Newtonian, = L exactly), i.e. up to 8.5% -- the whole kappa gap is recoverable, and SPARC spans this entire range

